      <h3 class="subsection-title">Introduction</h3>
      <p>This publication discusses two sets of rules that may limit the losses you can deduct on your tax return from any trade, business, rental, or other activity. These rules are designed to prevent taxpayers from claiming losses that are not supported by their economic reality. The second part discusses the at-risk rules. These rules are designed to prevent taxpayers from claiming losses from any activity, you must apply the at-risk rules to any activity that generates a loss. </p>
