    <div style="width: 45%;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Trade or Business Activities</h2>
      <p>A trade or business activity is an activity that:</p>
      <ul class="list-item">
        <li>Involves the conduct of a trade or business, or</li>
        <li>Is an activity in which the taxpayer materially participates.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Revenue Code section 162 of the Internal Revenue Code allows deductions for ordinary and necessary expenses paid or incurred in carrying on any trade or business. The rules in this publication apply to activities that are not considered trades or businesses.</p>
      <p>A taxpayer materially participates in an activity if they meet one of the seven tests listed in the regulations. If a taxpayer meets any one of these tests, the activity is considered a trade or business for tax purposes.</p>
      <p>You generally report trade or business losses on Schedule C, E, F, or in Part II of Form 1040.</p>
      <h3 class="subsection-title">Rental Activities</h3>
      <p>A rental activity is a passive activity if even if the taxpayer materially participates in the activity, the activity is not considered a trade or business. A rental activity is generally passive unless the taxpayer materially participates in the activity. A rental activity is considered a trade or business if the taxpayer materially participates in the activity.</p>
      <p>If you materially participate in a rental activity, you may be able to deduct losses from that activity, subject to other limitations.</p>
      <h3 class="subsection-title">Exceptions</h3>
      <p>Your activity is not a rental activity if any of the following apply:</p>
      <ul class="list-item">
        <li>The activity is a trade or business.</li>
        <li>The activity is a qualified rental activity.</li>
        <li>The activity is a real estate professional activity.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div style="width: 50%;">
        <h3 class="subsection-title">Who Must Use These Rules?</h3>
        <p>The passive activity rules apply to:</p>
        <ul class="list-item">
          <li>Individuals.</li>
          <li>Partnerships.</li>
          <li>Trusts.</li>
          <li>Corporations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Trusts, partnerships, and corporations must determine whether the activity is passive or not. The rules apply to the entity that is engaged in the activity.</p>
        <p>For information about personal service corporations, see Publication 563. For information about other entities, see Publication 563.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 45%;">
        <h3 class="subsection-title">Passive Activities</h3>
        <p>There are two kinds of passive activities:</p>
        <ul class="list-item">
          <li>Trade or business activities in which you do not materially participate.</li>
          <li>Rental activities.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A trade or business activity is passive if you do not materially participate in the activity.</p>
        <p>A rental activity is passive unless you materially participate in the activity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

